   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "Being busy is the most comfortable way to stay exactly where you are.",
     "mode": "story",
     "pause": 0.5,
     "gains": [
      1.1
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "It feels like progress.",
     "mode": "quote",
     "pause": 0.6
    },
    {
     "text": "Emails answered. Meetings attended. A to-do list full of checkmarks.",
     "mode": "story",
     "pause": 0.5
    },
    {
     "text": "You go to bed exhausted, so it must have been a good day.",
     "mode": "normal",
     "pause": 0.6
    },
    {
     "text": "But look at what actually moved.",
     "mode": "quote",
     "pause": 0.7
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "b",
   "at": "auto",
   "gap": 0.8,
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "Nothing important did.",
     "mode": "quote",
     "pause": 0.6
    },
    {
     "text": "Busy is motion. Progress is direction.",
     "mode": "quote",
     "pause": 0.9,
     "gains": [
      1.15
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Brian Tracy calls it the vital few: a handful of tasks create most of your results.",
     "mode": "normal",
     "pause": 0.6
    },
    {
     "text": "So tomorrow, before you answer anything, do the one task that actually moves you.",
     "mode": "normal",
     "pause": 0.6
    },
    {
     "text": "Less motion. More direction.",
     "mode": "quote",
     "pause": 1.0,
     "gains": [
